      ""rigor_of_approach_score"": 3,
      ""rigor_of_approach_justification"": ""The theoretical physics rigor is high, but the ML rigor is low. Merely stating 'build ML models' and asking NCEMS for architectural help is insufficient for an AI-focused proposal."",
      ""scope_and_timeline_score"": 3,
      ""scope_and_timeline_justification"": ""The timeline allocates too little time (Months 5-12) for the complex task of integrating DMS, MD, and building/training novel ML architectures."",
      ""synthesis_focus_score"": 2,
      ""synthesis_focus_justification"": ""Uses diverse datasets to synthesize a new model, but explicitly plans to generate new experimental data, violating a core tenet of the RFP."",
      ""data_identification_score"": 5,
      ""data_identification_justification"": ""Excellent identification of 28 specific proteins with matching DMS (MaveDB) and MD data (MDRepo/MDVerse), showing strong preliminary data scouting."",
      ""open_science_commitment_score"": 5,
      ""open_science_commitment_justification"": ""Clear commitment to releasing the AI models and the AllosteryMap tool, which will be a valuable resource for the community.""
    },
    {
      ""review_text"": ""I am reviewing this from the perspective of a structural biologist who studies transcription factors (TFs). The premise of understanding allostery dynamically rather than through static MWC/KNF discrete states is the correct modern view of the field. Applying this to TFs is a brilliant choice, as their regulation by small molecules or distal protein-protein interactions is notoriously difficult to capture via static crystallography. The inclusion of the Okafor lab, which has strong expertise in this area, is a huge plus. However, as an evaluator for the NCEMS data synthesis call, I must follow the strict rules of the RFP. The call states: 'It does not generate any new experimental data.' The proposal's plan to have the Okafor lab experimentally test designs via mutagenesis and biophysical assays is a fatal flaw for this specific funding mechanism. The PIs should submit this to a standard NSF or NIH mechanism, where computational-experimental feedback loops are praised. Here, it disqualifies the proposal from being a true synthesis project."",
      ""strengths"": ""Focuses on a highly relevant and challenging class of proteins (transcription factors); strong theoretical shift from static to dynamic allostery; well-composed interdisciplinary team."",
      ""weakness"": ""The proposal fundamentally misunderstands the nature of this specific RFP by including a significant wet-lab experimental component (Phase 3)."",
      ""overall_numeric_score"": 2,
      ""overall_summary"": ""Scientifically, this is a 5-star proposal that beautifully marries biophysics, ML, and structural biology. Unfortunately, administratively it is a 1-star proposal because it explicitly proposes generating new experimental data in a strict data-synthesis-only call."",
      ""relevance_to_emergent_phenomena_score"": 5,
      ""relevance_to_emergent_phenomena_justification"": ""Allosteric regulation in transcription factors is a prime example of an emergent molecular property crucial for cellular signaling."",
      ""novelty_and_significance_score"": 4,
      ""novelty_and_significance_justification"": ""Creating a quantifiable 'allostery score' that allows cross-species and cross-protein comparisons is highly novel."",
      ""rigor_of_approach_score"": 4,
      ""rigor_of_approach_justification"": ""The biophysical approach (fluctuation-response relationships, dynamic coupling) is extremely rigorous and well-established in the PI's prior work."",
      ""scope_and_timeline_score"": 2,
