}",0,y2::9,y2,9,Predictive Synthesis Framework for Elucidating Biophysical Cell State from Spatial Transcriptomics and Proteomics,Accepted,Jean Fan; Tai-yen Chen; Steve Presse,4,/Users/eveyhuang/Documents/NICO/human-AI-proposal/data/human-proposals/human-proposals-y2.json,False,,,,,,"From a physical and mathematical perspective, the proposal is solid. The team proposes using Large Deformation Diffeomorphic Metric Mapping (LDDMM) via STalign to handle the non-rigid deformations inherent in imaging adjacent tissue sections. The evaluation metrics for registration (Jacobian regularity, inverse-consistency, RMSD on landmarks) are rigorous, standard in statistical physics, and highly appropriate. My primary concern is the integration of the statistical physics components. The text mentions Dr. Presse will provide 'uncertainty quantification and correlation validation', but the actual proposal text does not detail how UQ will be embedded into the deep learning pipeline. Furthermore, the proposal lacks any mention of mentoring or workforce training, focusing entirely on PIs and staff scientists.",Rigorous mathematical foundation for image registration; well-defined physical evaluation metrics for patch correspondence.,Vague integration of statistical physics and UQ into the AI model; completely ignores the RFP requirement to train a data-savvy workforce.,4,"Mathematically rigorous framework for tissue registration with excellent evaluation metrics, though the integration of uncertainty quantification is underdeveloped and the training mandate is ignored.",4,The biophysical features extracted are relevant to understanding emergent cell states.,4,Applying diffeomorphic alignment to sub-cellular cross-modal omics is a significant technical advancement.,4,The mathematical controls and evaluation metrics for registration are exceptionally rigorous.,3,"Feasible timeline for the software pipeline, but penalized for completely omitting a trainee plan.",5,Brings together distinct physical and computational perspectives for data synthesis.,4,"Good identification of Spatch, which has the necessary metadata to support the registration tests.",4,"Commits to permissive licensing and reproducibility, though physical biophysical constraints could be better documented.",/Users/eveyhuang/Documents/NICO/human-AI-proposal/data/reviews/ai_reviews/baseline/ai_reviews_baseline_complete_20260709_143810.csv,gemini-3.1-pro-preview,0,review_neutralization_v1,2026-07-09T23:06:33.446219,0,success,,"The proposal presents a solid physical and mathematical framework, utilizing Large Deformation Diffeomorphic Metric Mapping and rigorous evaluation metrics to address non-rigid tissue deformations. However, the text lacks specific details regarding the integration of statistical physics and uncertainty quantification within the deep learning pipeline. Additionally, it does not address the solicitation's requirement for mentoring and workforce training.","The proposal demonstrates a rigorous mathematical foundation for image registration. It also employs well-defined, standard physical evaluation metrics to accurately assess patch correspondence.","The integration of statistical physics and uncertainty quantification into the artificial intelligence model is insufficiently detailed. Furthermore, the proposal fails to include required mentoring and workforce training components."
